# Icons

- `lucide-react` is the default everywhere, especially dense app/dashboard UI (`(app)` routes, tables,
  forms, nav). Keep using it there — don't replace existing lucide icons.
- `@phosphor-icons/react`, `duotone` weight, is for marketing/landing sections only (`home/`, hero,
  feature/pricing grids) where a richer two-tone icon fits the larger type and spacing.
- Never mix packs for the same concept in the same view. Never mix Phosphor weights in one section.
- Size icons via the `size-*` Tailwind utility (matches the existing `button.tsx` convention of
  `[&_svg:not([class*='size-'])]:size-4`), not raw `width`/`height` props.
